      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for catching this. Here is how we are going to use it (I also pasted this on b/194967894#comment2):\n\nTo identify call trace and determine whether they are duplicated, we leverage kernel function \"walk_stackframe\" to access return addresses of each call frame in a call trace, and use these (e.g.: hashing them) to compare call traces. With these information we can print a duplicated call trace only once in the log, and specify tasks that share this call trace, to save log buffer space.\n\nA rough example:\n\n\u003d Before \u003d\nTask A\n  schedule+0x60\n  wait_for_event+0x40\n  sys_wait++0x90  \nTask B\n  busy+0x8\n  fs_read_file+0x240\n  sys_read++0x8\nTask C\n  schedule+0x60\n  wait_for_event+0x40\n  sys_wait++0x90\n\n\u003d After \u003d\nTask A / Task C\n  schedule+0x60\n  wait_for_event+0x40\n  sys_wait++0x90  \nTask B\n  busy+0x8\n  fs_read_file+0x240\n  sys_read++0x8",
      "parentUuid": "3adf97d0_a7c0cf28",
